<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img class="bg" src="/assets/img/photos/contractors-plans.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/contractors-plans-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/contractors-plans.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.1"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/calculators-and-planners/">Tools</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Appraisal File Strength Score</span></nav><p class="kicker">Free checklist</p><h1>Appraisal File Strength Score</h1><p class="lede">Strong appraisals are built before anyone signs a demand. Answer twelve questions to see where your file stands and what to fix first.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Appraisal file strength score</span><i>12 questions · about two minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get written confirmation that coverage is accepted. If the claim was denied, talk to an Illinois attorney before considering appraisal."><span>Has the carrier accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask the adjuster in writing for the complete itemized estimate."><span>Do you have the carrier’s full line-item estimate, not just a summary?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get an independent line-item estimate — a one-line bid won’t carry weight with a panel."><span>Do you have your own itemized estimate from a contractor or estimator?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Collect every photo and note when each was taken. Add photos of current conditions."><span>Do you have dated photos taken soon after the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find ‘Appraisal’ in the policy conditions and note any timing rules."><span>Have you read the appraisal paragraph in your policy?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Suit Against Us’ condition and put the date on your calendar — our deadline calendar can help."><span>Have you calendared your policy’s suit-limitation date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make reasonable temporary repairs and keep every receipt."><span>Are temporary repairs done and receipts saved?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download or request the declarations page from your agent or carrier."><span>Do you have your current declarations page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure wet walls, attics, decking and basements have been inspected so the scope is complete."><span>Has hidden damage been opened up and documented?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Gather emails, letters and claim notes in date order."><span>Is your correspondence with the carrier saved in date order?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run the disputed amount estimator — a small gap may not justify appraisal costs."><span>Is the gap between estimates more than about 10% or $5,000?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="If a proof of loss was requested, return it on time."><span>If the carrier asked for a sworn proof of loss, has it been sent?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-reset>Reset answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out" aria-live="polite" style="grid-template-columns:minmax(220px,300px) 1fr;align-items:start">
      <div>
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#f3e7de" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#ff5f0f" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3" style="transition:stroke-dashoffset .5s,stroke .3s"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint" style="text-align:center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Your to-do list</p>
        <ul data-o="todo" style="margin:0;padding-left:1.1em"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></div>
<p class="hint center">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice, and nothing you type is stored.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>How it’s weighted</h2>
<p>Coverage, estimates and evidence carry the most weight because they decide whether appraisal is the right tool and how well your number will hold up. Paperwork items still matter but are easier to fix.</p>
<h2>Reading your score</h2>
<ul><li><strong>75 and up:</strong> a solid file. A professional review of the gap is the next step.</li>
<li><strong>45 to 74:</strong> finish the open items first; each one strengthens your position.</li>
<li><strong>Under 45:</strong> invoking appraisal now could lock in a low number. Build the file first.</li></ul>

<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is anything I enter saved?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>No. The score runs entirely in your browser and nothing is stored or sent.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I share my result?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Yes — take a screenshot of your score and to-do list and bring it to your consultation.</p></div></details></div>
